  "body": "## Vulnerability details\n\nWhile I was reviewing the reward distribution logic in GaugeCL, I notice a bug. The code fetches `clPool.rollover()` and adds it to calculate `totalRewardAmount`, then passes this value to `rewardReserve`. But when I looked at the `rewardRate` calculation, it only uses `rewardAmount`. That felt wrong.\n\nHere's the problematic section:\n\n```solidity\n// Line 251 in GaugeCL.sol\nuint256 totalRewardAmount = rewardAmount + clPool.rollover();\n\nif (block.timestamp >= _periodFinish) {\n    // Starting a new reward period\n    rewardRate = rewardAmount / epochTimeRemaining;  // <-- Bug here\n    clPool.syncReward({\n        rewardRate: rewardRate,\n        rewardReserve: totalRewardAmount,\n        periodFinish: epochEndTimestamp\n    });\n```\n\nI compared this to the else branch (when continuing an existing period):\n\n```solidity\n} else {\n    uint256 pendingRewards = epochTimeRemaining * rewardRate;\n    rewardRate = (rewardAmount + pendingRewards) / epochTimeRemaining;  // <-- Correctly includes pending\n    clPool.syncReward({\n        rewardRate: rewardRate,\n        rewardReserve: totalRewardAmount + pendingRewards,\n        periodFinish: epochEndTimestamp\n    });\n}\n```\n\nThe else branch properly includes `pendingRewards` in the rate calculation. So why doesn't the if branch include the rollover? They serve the same purpose - both represent undistributed rewards that should be part of the new rate.\n\n### What rollover actually is\n\nLooking at CLPool.sol, rollover accumulates when there's no staked liquidity to receive rewards:\n\n```solidity\nfunction _updateRewardsGrowthGlobal() internal {\n    // ...\n    if (stakedLiquidity > 0) {\n        rewardGrowthGlobalX128 += FullMath.mulDiv(reward, FixedPoint128.Q128, stakedLiquidity);\n    } else {\n        rollover += reward;  // Saved for when liquidity returns\n    }\n}\n```\n\nAnd here's the kicker - `syncReward()` explicitly deletes the rollover:\n\n```solidity\nfunction syncReward(...) external {\n    rewardRate = _rewardRate;\n    rewardReserve = _rewardReserve;\n    periodFinish = _periodFinish;\n    delete rollover;  // Expects rollover was included in the new rate\n}\n```\n\nIf rollover wasn't meant to be distributed in the new period, why delete it?\n\n### Impact breakdown\n\nLet's say Week 1 has no staked liquidity. All 1000 HYBR emissions roll over. Then Week 2 starts with liquidity staked and another 1000 HYBR comes in.\n\n**What should happen:**\n- Total available: 2000 HYBR (1000 new + 1000 rollover)\n- Rate: 2000 / 604800 seconds = 0.003306878 HYBR/sec\n- Distributed over week: 2000 HYBR \n\n**What actually happens:**\n- Total in reserve: 2000 HYBR (correctly set)\n- Rate: 1000 / 604800 seconds = 0.001653439 HYBR/sec (missing rollover!)\n- Distributed over week: 1000 HYBR\n- Undistributed: 1000 HYBR (becomes new rollover)\n\nUsers only get half the rewards they should. The rollover persists but never gets distributed because each new period makes the same mistake.\n\nI ran some math and realized if this pattern continues, rollover just grows infinitely. That's not sustainable and definitely breaks the emission model the protocol designed.\n\n**Paste the POC code below into C4Poc.t.sol and run the command `forge test --mt test_M01_RolloverNotIncludedInRateCalculation -vvv`\n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nSimple fix - just change line 256 to use `totalRewardAmount` instead of `rewardAmount`:\n\n```diff\n  uint256 totalRewardAmount = rewardAmount + clPool.rollover();\n\n  if (block.timestamp >= _periodFinish) {\n-     rewardRate = rewardAmount / epochTimeRemaining;\n+     rewardRate = totalRewardAmount / epochTimeRemaining;\n      clPool.syncReward({\n          rewardRate: rewardRate,\n          rewardReserve: totalRewardAmount,\n          periodFinish: epochEndTimestamp\n      });\n  }\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity 0.8.13;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {C4PoCTestbed} from \"./C4PoCTestbed.t.sol\";\n\ncontract C4PoC is C4PoCTestbed {\n    uint256 constant WEEKLY_EMISSION = 1000 * 1e18;\n    uint256 constant WEEK = 7 days;\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n    }\n\n    function test_submissionValidity() external {}\n\n    function test_M01_RolloverNotIncludedInRateCalculation() external {\n        // Week 1: No liquidity, all goes to rollover\n        uint256 week1Emission = WEEKLY_EMISSION;\n        uint256 rolloverFromWeek1 = week1Emission;\n        \n        // Week 2: Liquidity added, new emission arrives\n        uint256 week2Emission = WEEKLY_EMISSION;\n        uint256 totalRewardAmount = week2Emission + rolloverFromWeek1;\n        \n        uint256 epochTimeRemaining = WEEK;\n        \n        // What the rate SHOULD be (including rollover)\n        uint256 correctRewardRate = totalRewardAmount / epochTimeRemaining;\n        \n        // What the rate ACTUALLY is (buggy - missing rollover)\n        uint256 buggyRewardRate = week2Emission / epochTimeRemaining;\n        \n        // The buggy rate is exactly half what it should be\n        assertLt(buggyRewardRate, correctRewardRate);\n        assertEq(buggyRewardRate * 2, correctRewardRate);\n        \n        // Calculate what gets distributed over the week\n        uint256 totalAvailable = totalRewardAmount;\n        uint256 buggyDistributed = (buggyRewardRate * WEEK);\n        uint256 correctDistributed = (correctRewardRate * WEEK);\n        uint256 rolloverAfterWeek2 = totalAvailable - buggyDistributed;\n        \n        // Buggy version only distributes the new emission\n        assertApproxEqAbs(buggyDistributed, week2Emission, 1e6);\n        \n        // Correct version distributes everything\n        assertApproxEqAbs(correctDistributed, totalRewardAmount, 1e6);\n        \n        // Rollover persists instead of being cleared\n        assertApproxEqAbs(rolloverAfterWeek2, rolloverFromWeek1, 1e6);\n        \n        // The correct version distributes 2x more\n        assertGt(correctDistributed, buggyDistributed);\n        assertEq(correctDistributed, buggyDistributed * 2);\n    }\n}\n```\n\nRun with: `forge test --mt test_M01_RolloverNotIncludedInRateCalculation -vvv`",
